            <ArticleTitle>Intermittent subcutaneous opioids: using an algorithm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>477-82</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nurses and patients prefer the administration of injections via an indwelling subcutaneous cannula. Patients undergoing intermediate and minor surgery need improved pain relief. The algorithm provides a safe and acceptable mechanism for administering subcutaneous opioids more frequently.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
